WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.084 --> 00:00:02.044
[Annie] <i>Previously on</i> Sterling Point…

2
00:00:02.128 --> 00:00:04.422
[Marjorie] <i>So sorry</i>
<i>about your grandfather's passing.</i>

3
00:00:04.505 --> 00:00:06.132
Connor and Annie Jacobson.

4
00:00:06.215 --> 00:00:08.551
Gordon has made you
the beneficiaries of his trust.

5
00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:10.886
It includes a parcel of land in Canada.

6
00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.931
Gordon wrote us letters our entire lives.
Dad hid 'em in a safe.

7
00:00:14.014 --> 00:00:16.142
[Connor] <i>We're not even</i>
<i>biologically related.</i>

8
00:00:16.225 --> 00:00:18.811
The last letter that Gordon wrote.
he said. "Find her."

9
00:00:18.894 --> 00:00:21.439
-Find who?
-Exactly! Something's going on.

10
00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:23.399
We have to figure out what's happening.

11
00:00:23.482 --> 00:00:25.317
"Annie. find her." [sighs]

12
00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:30.906
-Annie? Hi. yeah. Ellis. your pilot.
-Hi.

13
00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.951
[Ellis] <i>Welcome to Sterling Point.</i>
<i>Old owner said he'd never rent it.</i>

14
00:00:34.034 --> 00:00:35.953
-[Annie] <i>You knew him?</i>
<i>-He owned this island.</i>

15
00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.246
[softly] Hey. Mom.

16
00:00:37.329 --> 00:00:39.373
Is it weird
that girl's renting Gord's cottage?

17
00:00:39.457 --> 00:00:41.667
What girl is renting his cottage?

18
00:00:42.793 --> 00:00:44.670
Wait. Annie? Annie Jacobson?

19
00:00:45.254 --> 00:00:46.255
[Annie] Rory.

20
00:00:46.338 --> 00:00:47.757
Wait. so why are you here?

21
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:49.049
My mom spent time here.

22
00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.342
<i>Actually. is your mom here?</i>

23
00:00:50.426 --> 00:00:52.219
-Hi.
-Oh. my. Annie Jacobson.

24
00:00:52.303 --> 00:00:55.222
Your mother. she was so upset.

25
00:00:55.306 --> 00:00:57.183
That's what finally led her to filing.

26
00:00:57.266 --> 00:00:59.268
For divorce from your dad.

27
00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.190
[gasps] Jesus!

28
00:01:05.316 --> 00:01:07.359
-Who are you?
-Who are you?

29
00:01:07.443 --> 00:01:09.612
What are you doing
in my grandfather's cottage?

30
00:01:15.659 --> 00:01:17.661
["H.E.R." playing]

31
00:02:15.302 --> 00:02:16.303
[Ramona] Hello?

32
00:02:38.993 --> 00:02:40.202
[gasps] Jesus!

33
00:02:42.121 --> 00:02:43.330
Who are you?

34
00:02:45.583 --> 00:02:46.417
Who are you?

35
00:02:47.793 --> 00:02:50.588
What the fuck are you doing
in my grandfather's cottage?

36
00:02:52.756 --> 00:02:54.049
-Hello?
-Sorry.

37
00:02:54.967 --> 00:02:58.137
Hi. Um. I-I…
I thought that this was my cottage.

38
00:02:58.220 --> 00:03:01.432
-You thought this was your cottage?
-I mean. my Airbnb.

39
00:03:01.515 --> 00:03:05.269
-Um. I'm so sorry. What is your name?
-I'm not telling you!

40
00:03:05.352 --> 00:03:07.563
What's your name?
Also. this isn't an Airbnb.

41
00:03:08.564 --> 00:03:10.024
How long have you been here?

42
00:03:10.733 --> 00:03:11.692
I just got here today.

43
00:03:11.775 --> 00:03:14.737
Then why is there hundreds of bottles
of stuff in the bathroom?

44
00:03:14.820 --> 00:03:15.821
Those are my creams.

45
00:03:17.823 --> 00:03:21.201
-Uh. sorry. My name's Annie.
-Yeah. Cool.

46
00:03:21.285 --> 00:03:24.747
Nice to meet you. Annie. Pack up your shit
and leave now. I won't press charges.

47
00:03:24.830 --> 00:03:25.915
Jesus Christ.

48
00:03:27.708 --> 00:03:30.169
[objects clattering]

49
00:03:32.838 --> 00:03:33.881
[softly] Oh. my God.

50
00:03:34.590 --> 00:03:36.675
[breath trembling]

51
00:03:58.822 --> 00:04:03.118
I noticed that you look a lot like
the woman in the pictures on the wall.

52
00:04:04.912 --> 00:04:07.665
That's a very creepy thing to say
right now. I'm not gonna lie.

53
00:04:07.748 --> 00:04:08.874
Totally.

54
00:04:09.667 --> 00:04:12.252
I'm sorry. I meant that as a compliment.
Like. you guys are…

55
00:04:13.128 --> 00:04:14.171
both so pretty.

56
00:04:17.424 --> 00:04:18.300
Are you related?

57
00:04:18.801 --> 00:04:19.802
[Ramona] Kinda.

58
00:04:22.054 --> 00:04:22.888
She's my mom.

59
00:04:25.516 --> 00:04:27.434
There aren't any Airbnbs on the island.

60
00:04:27.518 --> 00:04:30.062
-so you should start at Port Carling.
-Wait! Sorry.

61
00:04:30.145 --> 00:04:33.649
Is there no way I can chill here tonight.
and we can discuss this in the morning?

62
00:04:33.732 --> 00:04:36.068
That's a "Fuck no." Uh-uh.

63
00:04:36.151 --> 00:04:39.321
Can we please talk about this
for a second? This is a little bit crazy.

64
00:04:39.405 --> 00:04:40.364
Are you kicking me out

65
00:04:40.447 --> 00:04:41.949
-in the middle of the night?
-Yeah.

66
00:04:42.032 --> 00:04:44.034
-I can provide a background check.
-Don't care.

67
00:04:44.118 --> 00:04:47.413
[Annie] Oh! What the fuck? I thought
Canadians were supposed to be friendly.

68
00:04:47.496 --> 00:04:48.956
-[Ramona] Not true.
-[slams door]

69
00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.295
Okay.

70
00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:02.177
[Annie sobbing]

71
00:05:07.975 --> 00:05:10.144
-[softly] Jesus Christ.
-[sobbing continues]

72
00:05:12.354 --> 00:05:14.273
-Dude. you do not have to cry.
-I…

73
00:05:15.232 --> 00:05:18.652
I can cry if I want. I actually have
a lot to cry about right now. so…

74
00:05:23.574 --> 00:05:27.202
What's your full name. so I can google
your background check?

75
00:05:29.371 --> 00:05:30.289
It's. um…

76
00:05:31.206 --> 00:05:32.374
Annie Jacobson.

77
00:05:37.463 --> 00:05:39.506
-You gonna tell me yours?
-No.

78
00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:40.591
Okay.

79
00:05:40.674 --> 00:05:42.843
[Ramona] You can sleep on the couch
for one night.

80
00:05:42.926 --> 00:05:44.386
I'll feel bad if a bear eats you.

81
00:05:44.636 --> 00:05:46.346
But you have to be gone in the morning.

82
00:05:47.681 --> 00:05:50.309
Thank you so much. Thank you so much.

83
00:05:50.893 --> 00:05:53.062
I can't tell you
how much I appreciate this.

84
00:06:22.174 --> 00:06:24.426
Um. is your mom coming too.
by any chance?

85
00:06:26.011 --> 00:06:28.055
Is your mom coming? What…

86
00:06:28.806 --> 00:06:31.183
Or are you just airbnb-ing an island
in Canada alone?

87
00:06:31.266 --> 00:06:34.019
-What kinda question is that?
-Well. my mom is dead. so…

88
00:06:37.147 --> 00:06:37.981
Sorry.

89
00:06:38.816 --> 00:06:40.901
No. sorry. It's fine. It was. like. a…

90
00:06:42.069 --> 00:06:43.070
long time ago.

91
00:06:49.993 --> 00:06:50.953
My name is Ramona.

92
00:06:54.331 --> 00:06:55.541
My mom is dead too.

93
00:07:00.629 --> 00:07:01.755
[exhales softly]

94
00:07:24.111 --> 00:07:25.154
[exhales]

95
00:07:25.237 --> 00:07:26.321
[beeps]

96
00:07:26.405 --> 00:07:28.323
[softly] Connor. call me. period.

97
00:07:28.407 --> 00:07:31.326
There's a girl here
who looks just like Mom. exclamation mark.

98
00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:34.580
I'm freaking the fuck out.
Did Mom have a secret bio daughter?

99
00:07:34.663 --> 00:07:36.540
Question mark.
question mark. question mark.

100
00:07:37.499 --> 00:07:39.585
[text message chiming]

101
00:07:40.335 --> 00:07:44.506
And so much drama re Mom and Dad. period.

102
00:07:44.590 --> 00:07:46.800
and. quote. Grandpa. end quote.

103
00:07:47.759 --> 00:07:51.346
-[phone beeps]
-[text message chiming]

104
00:07:53.182 --> 00:07:57.853
Fuck. Why are all these going green?
Exclamation point. exclamation point.

105
00:07:58.228 --> 00:08:00.022
[phone beeps]

106
00:08:20.792 --> 00:08:22.544
I didn't even download <i>Love Island.</i>

107
00:08:34.973 --> 00:08:36.767
It's so fucking dark.

108
00:08:50.489 --> 00:08:51.782
[creaks]

109
00:09:18.976 --> 00:09:21.979
-["Deck the Halls" chiming on clock]
-[gasps]

110
00:09:30.195 --> 00:09:31.405
[exhales anxiously]

111
00:09:41.081 --> 00:09:42.874
[grunts] Fuck!

112
00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:45.377
You said you'd be gone by morning.
It's morning.

113
00:09:45.460 --> 00:09:46.628
Was that really necessary?

114
00:09:46.712 --> 00:09:48.922
-You better be gone when I'm back.
-[door slams]

115
00:10:00.142 --> 00:10:01.101
Awesome.

116
00:10:05.564 --> 00:10:07.566
["Back on You" playing]

117
00:10:31.423 --> 00:10:32.299
Come on.

118
00:10:35.218 --> 00:10:37.054
I just need one fucking bar.

119
00:10:47.230 --> 00:10:48.231
Okay.

120
00:10:52.486 --> 00:10:54.071
Okay. This is fine.

121
00:10:54.613 --> 00:10:55.739
All good.

122
00:10:58.617 --> 00:11:00.952
-[engine revving in distance]
-Whoa. [chuckles softly]

123
00:11:01.036 --> 00:11:01.912
Oh. fuck!

124
00:11:04.373 --> 00:11:05.874
Shit. Oh. shit.

125
00:11:05.957 --> 00:11:08.794
Shit. Shit. shit. shit. shit. Oh!

126
00:11:09.378 --> 00:11:10.212
Oh. shit.

127
00:11:11.671 --> 00:11:13.215
Fuck. fuck. fuck.

128
00:11:15.967 --> 00:11:17.803
Okay. Okay.

129
00:11:21.306 --> 00:11:22.766
Does this not do anything?

130
00:11:26.728 --> 00:11:27.729
Shit. shit. Fuck!

131
00:11:28.563 --> 00:11:30.148
[exclaims] Oh. fuck.

132
00:11:30.649 --> 00:11:32.567
Oh. fuck! Fuck.

133
00:11:35.112 --> 00:11:36.530
Oh. shit. [grunts]

134
00:11:37.906 --> 00:11:39.408
No! No. no. no.

135
00:11:40.158 --> 00:11:41.159
No. no. no!

136
00:11:41.243 --> 00:11:42.786
["Mr. Eclectic" playing]

137
00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:48.166
Fuck!

138
00:11:49.042 --> 00:11:51.128
Fuck me. Fuck!

139
00:11:52.421 --> 00:11:53.880
Yes. yes.

140
00:11:54.881 --> 00:11:55.757
No!

141
00:11:57.843 --> 00:11:58.885
Oh. Don't!

142
00:12:00.178 --> 00:12:01.555
Don't run me over!

143
00:12:02.055 --> 00:12:02.889
[Rory] Hey!

144
00:12:06.435 --> 00:12:07.769
-Hey!
-What's up?

145
00:12:08.937 --> 00:12:10.188
Fancy seeing you here.

146
00:12:10.772 --> 00:12:13.817
Okay. I know what this looks like.

147
00:12:14.484 --> 00:12:18.864
It's a classic "man rescuing a woman
from a near-death experience."

148
00:12:18.947 --> 00:12:20.115
Yeah. No. it's not…

149
00:12:20.740 --> 00:12:22.075
Not exactly what this is.

150
00:12:22.159 --> 00:12:25.620
-It's fine. I'll just swim home.
-No. No. Uh…

151
00:12:27.414 --> 00:12:28.415
I got this.

152
00:12:30.083 --> 00:12:31.209
-Amazing.
-Okay?

153
00:12:31.293 --> 00:12:32.669
-Life's good.
-Okay.

154
00:12:32.752 --> 00:12:34.379
Everything's going to plan.

155
00:12:35.046 --> 00:12:36.339
Right here. Go long.

156
00:12:59.237 --> 00:13:00.906
Yo. you need help?

157
00:13:00.989 --> 00:13:03.241
Don't break your back. You're old.

158
00:13:03.909 --> 00:13:07.037
-I am not that old. for God's sake.
-[chuckles]

159
00:13:07.621 --> 00:13:11.124
-I didn't know you were comin' up.
-Did you think I'd just dip forever?

160
00:13:11.208 --> 00:13:14.044
Well. I would hope not. but I had no idea.

161
00:13:14.127 --> 00:13:15.295
So it's really…

162
00:13:15.378 --> 00:13:16.505
[Ramona] Yeah. I'm here.

163
00:13:16.588 --> 00:13:18.048
And…

164
00:13:18.173 --> 00:13:20.675
not going anywhere. so get used to it.

165
00:13:21.343 --> 00:13:23.345
-[Joe] Hey. Ramona. wait. Listen.
-Yeah.

166
00:13:23.929 --> 00:13:26.056
All right. if you need anything. will you…

167
00:13:26.973 --> 00:13:30.143
I won't. But thank you for the concern.

168
00:13:36.483 --> 00:13:40.195
[Sully] All right. all right. all right.
Okay. GF and DF for Maple.

169
00:13:40.278 --> 00:13:43.031
-My God. Yum. Thank you.
-[Sully] No salsa verde for Ellis.

170
00:13:43.114 --> 00:13:45.325
-[Ellis] Thank you!
-[Ramona] Extra cheese on mine.

171
00:13:45.408 --> 00:13:46.660
by any chance?

172
00:13:46.743 --> 00:13:48.078
No? [exhales]

173
00:13:48.578 --> 00:13:50.539
Ouch! Sully. what did I ever do to you?

174
00:13:52.999 --> 00:13:54.668
Guys. it's a joke.

175
00:13:55.252 --> 00:13:57.254
What the fuck happened to you
while I was gone?

176
00:13:57.837 --> 00:13:59.130
Ramona. what?

177
00:13:59.214 --> 00:14:00.090
Oh. my God!

178
00:14:00.173 --> 00:14:01.508
-Hi!
-Hey!

179
00:14:01.591 --> 00:14:03.843
Like. can I touch you? Are you real?

180
00:14:03.927 --> 00:14:05.512
You are real. Hello. Oh. my God!

181
00:14:05.595 --> 00:14:07.681
-I can't even… When did you get here?
-Yeah.

182
00:14:07.764 --> 00:14:10.141
-Last night.
-And you didn't tell us? Why?

183
00:14:10.225 --> 00:14:11.810
'Cause I got back last night!

184
00:14:11.893 --> 00:14:14.145
-We're good.
-Oh. my God. Are you staying? Oi.

185
00:14:14.980 --> 00:14:17.649
I don't know.
Depends on if I still have a job.

186
00:14:18.650 --> 00:14:22.737
I mean. you've criminally overused
your vacation days. but whatever.

187
00:14:22.821 --> 00:14:24.906
-So. that's a yes.
-[all chuckle]

188
00:14:25.490 --> 00:14:27.534
Um. I'm actually so sorry.
I didn't get you one.

189
00:14:27.617 --> 00:14:30.662
And I know yours gets extra cheese.
Everyone knows that. So I'm sorry.

190
00:14:30.745 --> 00:14:32.205
Hey. you gorgeous little freak.

191
00:14:32.289 --> 00:14:35.208
Stop apologizing for everything.
It's fine. You're perfect.

192
00:14:35.292 --> 00:14:37.210
You don't have to apologize
ever again. okay?

193
00:14:37.294 --> 00:14:39.754
-Yeah. Not even a problem. Sorry.
-Yeah. You're fine.

194
00:14:39.838 --> 00:14:41.798
-What? Whoa! Thanks.
-Welcome back.

195
00:14:41.881 --> 00:14:42.757
Thanks.

196
00:14:43.341 --> 00:14:45.218
-What are these?
-Oh. they're shirts.

197
00:14:45.302 --> 00:14:47.220
-That's right. Marina--
-Oh. my God!

198
00:14:47.304 --> 00:14:48.638
-Marina…
-Marina Crew.

199
00:14:50.223 --> 00:14:51.600
["Off the Rails" playing]

200
00:14:52.267 --> 00:14:53.518
Whoo!

201
00:14:59.399 --> 00:15:00.358
Jump!

202
00:15:08.908 --> 00:15:09.826
[chuckles]

203
00:15:20.754 --> 00:15:22.714
-[gasps]
-[all laughing]

204
00:15:22.797 --> 00:15:23.673
[Sully] No!

205
00:15:26.217 --> 00:15:28.970
-Catch it next time. please.
-I'll try my best. Thank you.

206
00:15:29.763 --> 00:15:30.889
How do I look?

207
00:15:30.972 --> 00:15:32.223
-All right.
-Okay.

208
00:15:33.224 --> 00:15:34.559
-Got it?
-Yep.

209
00:15:37.187 --> 00:15:38.521
You know. I called you.

210
00:15:39.439 --> 00:15:40.523
Like. a lot.

211
00:15:41.149 --> 00:15:43.610
Sorry. It's actually
a lot harder than you'd think.

212
00:15:43.693 --> 00:15:45.236
taking care of a dying old man.

213
00:15:48.323 --> 00:15:49.324
Ramona. I…

214
00:15:51.201 --> 00:15:52.577
I was really worried about you.

215
00:15:53.495 --> 00:15:54.954
And I missed you. man.

216
00:15:57.582 --> 00:15:58.667
I'm glad you're back.

217
00:16:04.798 --> 00:16:08.134
And I'm really sorry you had to
go through all of that by yourself.

218
00:16:10.470 --> 00:16:11.721
Yeah. I'm fine now.

219
00:16:12.722 --> 00:16:13.682
Thanks.

220
00:16:16.184 --> 00:16:18.186
So. like. who's taking care of you?

221
00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:21.606
I mean.

222
00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.066
me. [chuckles]

223
00:16:24.275 --> 00:16:26.152
-You know how it is.
-Mmm.

224
00:16:27.487 --> 00:16:30.615
Gordon set you up with everything
that you need and everything?

225
00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:33.076
Yeah. I mean.

226
00:16:33.910 --> 00:16:36.246
I have the cottage and the island and…

227
00:16:39.332 --> 00:16:40.750
Everything. I'm good.

228
00:16:41.918 --> 00:16:43.169
-Okay.
-Yeah.

229
00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:00.270
You look so good.

230
00:17:00.353 --> 00:17:02.981
-In your mom's clothes?
-Okay. Yeah. that's weird.

231
00:17:03.064 --> 00:17:05.024
-But it's perfect for the party.
-Party?

232
00:17:05.108 --> 00:17:06.818
No party. Gathering.

233
00:17:06.901 --> 00:17:09.612
-Okay.
-Super low-key. Super casual vibes.

234
00:17:09.696 --> 00:17:11.448
-I'll let you get settled.
-Oh. yeah. I…

235
00:17:11.531 --> 00:17:14.492
Do you guys have service here?
I need to call Connor about something.

236
00:17:14.576 --> 00:17:16.828
-Yeah. you can use the Starlink.
-Oh!

237
00:17:16.911 --> 00:17:19.831
-Thank you so much.
-Yes. I will give you some privacy.

238
00:17:19.914 --> 00:17:21.374
-Thank you.
-All right.

239
00:17:22.625 --> 00:17:24.252
-Bye.
-[door closes]

240
00:17:25.879 --> 00:17:26.796
Okay.

241
00:17:28.506 --> 00:17:29.507
Do I…

242
00:17:29.591 --> 00:17:32.260
Do I wanna add a farm-fresh egg on top?

243
00:17:32.343 --> 00:17:33.970
[tutting]

244
00:17:34.763 --> 00:17:35.764
Yeah. why not?

245
00:17:36.473 --> 00:17:37.807
[cell phone buzzing]

246
00:17:37.891 --> 00:17:38.892
Oh. my God.

247
00:17:39.350 --> 00:17:40.977
What do you want? You're so annoying.

248
00:17:41.060 --> 00:17:43.396
I lost my entire order
from 4 Charles to pick this up.

249
00:17:43.480 --> 00:17:45.356
-Wait. you're home?
<i>-Yeah.</i>

250
00:17:45.440 --> 00:17:46.983
-Oh. she dumped you?
<i>-Shut up.</i>

