00:30:23.489 --> 00:30:26.742
Yeah. this place looks totally
like my place. I get it.

495
00:30:26.825 --> 00:30:27.993
-Yeah.
-I can explain this.

496
00:30:28.077 --> 00:30:29.453
-Oh. you can explain?
-Yes.

497
00:30:29.537 --> 00:30:31.372
I'd love for you to explain why you lied.

498
00:30:31.455 --> 00:30:33.499
-why you know my grandfather's name…
-Ramona--

499
00:30:33.582 --> 00:30:37.711
…why you broke into my cottage
and stole a photo of my dead mother.

500
00:30:37.795 --> 00:30:39.171
why the fuck you're here?

501
00:30:39.255 --> 00:30:40.589
I can honestly explain--

502
00:30:40.673 --> 00:30:43.801
-Why'd you steal a photo of my dead mom?
-'Cause she's my mother too!

503
00:30:46.971 --> 00:30:48.013
What did you just say?

504
00:30:48.097 --> 00:30:50.474
She's my mother too. [sighs]

505
00:30:51.809 --> 00:30:54.353
And I don't know anything that's going on.

506
00:30:55.813 --> 00:30:57.856
but I think that we might be sisters.

507
00:30:57.940 --> 00:30:59.692
Oh. shit.

508
00:31:05.114 --> 00:31:06.740
-Get in the boat.
-Why?

509
00:31:06.824 --> 00:31:08.367
-Just get in.
-[Annie] Okay.

510
00:31:20.296 --> 00:31:22.256
That girl is not gonna kill her. right?

511
00:31:22.881 --> 00:31:23.882
No.

512
00:31:26.051 --> 00:31:27.261
No.

513
00:31:29.138 --> 00:31:31.098
I'm almost positive that's a no.

514
00:31:36.854 --> 00:31:38.981
-You guys will check on Annie?
-Yeah. we got it.

515
00:31:48.198 --> 00:31:51.827
Is there a small part of you
that isn't sure Ramona won't kill her?

516
00:31:55.789 --> 00:31:57.207
-Yeah.
-Same. Okay. let's go.

517
00:32:10.429 --> 00:32:12.931
[Annie] I'm sorry. would you mind
slowing down a little?

518
00:32:13.015 --> 00:32:14.350
Okay. okay.

519
00:32:14.975 --> 00:32:16.143
We're gonna hit that.

520
00:32:17.519 --> 00:32:18.771
Fuck!

521
00:32:20.272 --> 00:32:21.857
Tell me everything you know.

522
00:32:22.858 --> 00:32:23.942
-Okay. Um…
-Now.

523
00:32:24.026 --> 00:32:26.737
Okay. Goldie was… is my mom.

524
00:32:27.237 --> 00:32:28.614
Uh. my adoptive mom.

525
00:32:28.697 --> 00:32:31.575
And she and my dad adopted me
and my twin brother. Connor.

526
00:32:31.659 --> 00:32:32.826
when we were newborns.

527
00:32:33.285 --> 00:32:36.288
Uh. and then she died of cancer
when we were two. and…

528
00:32:36.372 --> 00:32:39.583
um. I never knew anything
about this place or you.

529
00:32:40.709 --> 00:32:42.378
Then a lawyer called when Gordon died.

530
00:32:42.461 --> 00:32:45.881
and I found a letter that said.
"Find her." which I'm now assuming is you.

531
00:32:45.964 --> 00:32:48.842
And my dad was acting really weird.

532
00:32:48.926 --> 00:32:51.095
which made me so suspicious
that I decided…

533
00:32:51.970 --> 00:32:56.016
I decided that I would just come here
and see it for myself.

534
00:32:56.100 --> 00:32:59.103
And then I saw you.
and you looked so much like her

535
00:32:59.812 --> 00:33:01.146
that I knew

536
00:33:02.398 --> 00:33:04.024
that you were her daughter too.

537
00:33:07.319 --> 00:33:08.445
Did you know about me?

538
00:33:11.615 --> 00:33:12.616
No.

539
00:33:16.995 --> 00:33:19.665
Great. So. like. everyone's been
lying to us our whole life.

540
00:33:21.959 --> 00:33:24.002
That's actually. like. so fucked up.

541
00:33:27.840 --> 00:33:29.633
Why would they wanna keep us apart?

542
00:33:31.468 --> 00:33:32.469
We're sisters.

543
00:33:41.812 --> 00:33:43.147
You said you were adopted?

544
00:33:44.022 --> 00:33:45.023
Yeah.

545
00:33:50.779 --> 00:33:51.905
So we're not related.

546
00:33:53.782 --> 00:33:55.200
You're not my sister.

547
00:34:00.205 --> 00:34:01.665
You go back to New York now.

548
00:34:02.750 --> 00:34:04.334
Forever would be ideal.

549
00:34:22.394 --> 00:34:23.395
Hey.

550
00:34:23.479 --> 00:34:24.897
-Hey.
-I was looking for you.

551
00:34:25.397 --> 00:34:28.358
-Hey. [chuckles]
-Um…

552
00:34:28.442 --> 00:34:30.402
-How bad was it?
-Um…

553
00:34:31.737 --> 00:34:33.530
I would describe it as. like…

554
00:34:35.741 --> 00:34:36.742
soul-crushing.

555
00:34:37.201 --> 00:34:38.452
[sighs] Fuck.

556
00:34:39.077 --> 00:34:40.871
-She hates me.
-What?

557
00:34:40.954 --> 00:34:45.042
-[chuckles sadly] Yeah.
-No. she doesn't. okay? Ramona is…

558
00:34:46.418 --> 00:34:47.920
She's complicated.

559
00:34:48.962 --> 00:34:53.509
She's had a pretty rough year…
or rough couple of years. actually.

560
00:34:53.592 --> 00:34:58.305
Gordon was her only family.
Now she's alone. you know?

561
00:35:01.934 --> 00:35:05.103
Sorry. I didn't mean. like…
I didn't mean you're not her family.

562
00:35:05.187 --> 00:35:06.563
-Sorry. I meant--
-No.

563
00:35:06.647 --> 00:35:08.690
-I didn't take it that way at all.
-Okay. Sorry.

564
00:35:09.858 --> 00:35:12.110
No. you're good. you're good.
Yeah. [chuckles]

565
00:35:12.528 --> 00:35:13.821
I mean. we're not really. so…

566
00:35:17.950 --> 00:35:19.243
Where's her dad?

567
00:35:21.787 --> 00:35:23.455
Just never really been in the picture.

568
00:35:24.540 --> 00:35:27.876
Apparently. he was this random tourist
who Goldie had a fling with.

569
00:35:30.671 --> 00:35:32.756
Like. while she was married to my dad?

570
00:35:32.840 --> 00:35:34.216
That just. like…

571
00:35:36.009 --> 00:35:38.846
I'm sorry. That just does not sound like
my mom at all.

572
00:35:38.929 --> 00:35:44.226
Like. to have an affair with a random guy
and then never tell…

573
00:35:44.309 --> 00:35:47.646
Like. not tell your husband that you have
another daughter? That's. like…

574
00:35:52.401 --> 00:35:54.778
I guess I don't really
know my mom at all. though. so…

575
00:35:54.862 --> 00:35:56.864
[chuckles nervously]
what the fuck do I know?

576
00:36:01.410 --> 00:36:03.954
I think there's probably
a lot more to the story. right?

577
00:36:05.330 --> 00:36:06.331
Like. should I…

578
00:36:07.416 --> 00:36:10.836
[hesitates] I don't really know
what to do.

579
00:36:13.922 --> 00:36:15.674
Do you think I should just leave?

580
00:36:16.967 --> 00:36:19.094
Do you feel like you got
the answers you wanted?

581
00:36:21.346 --> 00:36:23.307
I feel like I've barely
scratched the surface.

582
00:36:25.434 --> 00:36:26.727
Maybe that's your answer.

583
00:36:34.693 --> 00:36:35.861
[Ramona] Don't come in.

584
00:36:40.699 --> 00:36:43.702
I found it in his briefcase after he died.

585
00:36:45.078 --> 00:36:47.831
and I just haven't gotten myself
to open it.

586
00:36:48.665 --> 00:36:51.877
And now I feel like I have to.
'cause she said she got a letter too…

587
00:36:53.170 --> 00:36:55.255
So. no. Sorry.

588
00:36:55.797 --> 00:36:59.301
You don't have to open it
just 'cause she's opened a letter.

589
00:37:00.594 --> 00:37:03.931
Yeah. but what if it says something
about her or…

590
00:37:04.431 --> 00:37:05.432
I mean. it might.

591
00:37:08.644 --> 00:37:11.396
[sighs] Why can't I open it?

592
00:37:12.940 --> 00:37:16.860
Because it's the last unopened letter
that you'll ever get from your grandpa.

593
00:37:18.070 --> 00:37:19.780
Of course you don't wanna read it.

594
00:37:20.530 --> 00:37:21.365
It's sad.

595
00:37:26.912 --> 00:37:27.955
It's a lot.

596
00:37:35.337 --> 00:37:36.380
You read it.

597
00:37:37.005 --> 00:37:38.006
What?

598
00:37:38.090 --> 00:37:40.884
Don't read it out loud.
Just read it in your head and then…

599
00:37:41.593 --> 00:37:44.596
I don't know. I can gauge from the look
on your face if I can read it.

600
00:37:44.680 --> 00:37:46.682
Wait. are you sure?

601
00:37:46.765 --> 00:37:50.769
Yes. It's okay. I swear. It's okay.
I won't freak out on you.

602
00:38:13.959 --> 00:38:14.793
What?

603
00:38:14.876 --> 00:38:16.712
Do you want me to tell you?

604
00:38:16.795 --> 00:38:20.632
No. I just… Is it bad?
'Cause it seems like it's bad.

605
00:38:21.133 --> 00:38:22.467
-Is it--
-You should read it.

606
00:38:26.596 --> 00:38:29.599
No. Mmm-mmm.

607
00:38:31.143 --> 00:38:33.812
Annie is not lying.

608
00:38:36.106 --> 00:38:39.401
My mom had one daughter.
and that was me. She--

609
00:38:39.484 --> 00:38:42.696
That girl did not even know her.
There's no way.

610
00:38:42.779 --> 00:38:44.698
I know. I know.

611
00:38:45.657 --> 00:38:48.994
But. Ramona. you didn't know her either.

612
00:38:58.336 --> 00:38:59.379
Right. Yeah.

613
00:38:59.463 --> 00:39:02.466
["Sequence 02" playing]

614
00:39:20.108 --> 00:39:21.318
I think I got it from here.

615
00:39:22.694 --> 00:39:24.738
Sure? I don't mind. like…

616
00:39:24.821 --> 00:39:26.448
Yeah. Thank you.

617
00:39:30.368 --> 00:39:31.369
Yeah.

618
00:40:01.942 --> 00:40:03.735
Are you coming or not?

619
00:40:47.154 --> 00:40:50.157
[dramatic music playing]
